# Cursor rules — short form
# Read AGENTS.md before any non-trivial change.
# This file is a compact reminder for inline completion; AGENTS.md is the
# single source of truth.

# === ARCHITECTURE ===
# Three layers: Probe (ProbingWrapper / SystemPingWrapper / TCPPingWrapper /
# ErrorWrapper) -> PingService + HostRepository -> TUI / StatusServer / Display.
# Wrappers never reach into the repository. UI never mutates wrappers.
# PingService is the only owner of Start/Stop.

# === CONCURRENCY ===
# PWStats mutations MUST hold the wrapper mutex. Stats() and CalcStats()
# return value copies — never return *w.stats.
# updateStatsCache() is the only place CalcStats() is called per tick.
# getCachedStats() returns empty PWStats on miss, never blocks.
# Stop() is idempotent (sync.Once). goroutines exit on stop within 1 tick.
# No DNS in Start() — use DNSUpdater (3s initial, 60s period, 500ms lookup).

# === STATE MACHINE ===
# PWStats.ComputeState(timeout) is the only place state flips.
# Never mutate skip_next_up_highlight, loss_reference_recv,
# last_up_transition, has_ever_been_online, last_loss_nano,
# last_loss_duration outside ComputeState.

# === LIMITS (do not change without justification) ===
# maxExpandedCIDRHosts=65536, onceWorkerLimit=100, startup sem=20,
# DNS sem=20, traceSem=2, maxTraceStates=256,
# maxViewPatchBytes=1MiB, maxHiddenViewItems=10000,
# maxHiddenKeyLength=512, dnsTimeout=500ms, dnsCache positive=1h,
# dnsCache negative=5m, adaptive slow interval=10s, adaptive threshold=12s.

# === CONVENTIONS ===
# snake_case struct fields. Early returns. Idempotent Stop.
# ErrorWrapper for any unresolvable host — never exit().
# Test files: *_test.go next to the file under test.
# Reference tests: lifecycle_regression_test.go (countingWrapper, MockWrapper).
# For time-dependent tests, use nowFunc (package-level var in pwstats.go).

# === FORBIDDEN ===
# panic in wrapper goroutines
# DNS in Start()
# Returning *w.stats
# Adding a top-level dep without checking stdlib + existing deps first
# Mixing refactors with behavior changes in one commit
# Bypassing HostRepository from anywhere
# Mutating PWStats state-machine fields outside ComputeState

# === BUILD TAGS ===
# pinger_tcp_win.go uses //go:build windows.
# pinger_tcp.go is //go:build !windows.

# === HOST PARSING ===
# Regex: ^(tcp|ip)([46])?://(\[?.+?\]?)(?::(\d+))?$
# IPv6 needs brackets: tcp://[::1]:22.

# === AUTO-FALLBACK ===
# probePureGoAllowed() in main.go probes 127.0.0.1 once on startup;
# if "permission" / "operation not permitted" appears, fall back to -s.

# === WHEN DONE ===
# - go build ./...
# - go test ./...
# - update README.md / docs/ as needed
# - never commit without the vendor diff when go.mod changed